  "problem": "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{\u2032}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t)=\u27e8\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t}{{e}^{t}},\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t}{{e}^{t}}\u27e9,\\,{T}^{\u2032}(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\u27e8-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
